# Edge cases and regressions

Treat the unhappy paths as part of the task, not a follow-up.

Check the states this product actually has:

- Signed out, waitlist, and invited sign-in.
- No team selected (`Choose your team`) and a team selected.
- Empty data, `setup_required`, and a failed refresh that must keep the last painted board.
- Student chrome versus owner or admin chrome.
- Phone width and desktop width when layout or navigation changed.
- Offline or last-snapshot behavior when the screen is supposed to keep working without venue Wi-Fi.

After the change, open the neighboring route that shares the shell, hub tab, or data. Confirm its primary action, empty state, and navigation still behave as they did.

Do not claim a path is fine if you did not open it.
